6) How to prepare in the next 2 months
- Keep a dated parenting log: exchanges, missed visits, important incidents, who was present.
- Gather and organize the financial documents above.
- Save all communications with the other parent (texts, emails, voicemail logs).
- Avoid unilateral major changes (moving the child, changing school, international travel) without discussing with your attorney or obtaining court permission.
- Consider whether mediation or collaborative negotiation is acceptable to you; discuss boundaries with your attorney.
- Discuss safety plan if there are any domestic violence concerns (protective orders, supervised exchanges, law enforcement notifications).

7) If there are urgent or safety issues
- Ask your attorney whether a temporary emergency order or protective order is appropriate now.
- If there is immediate danger to you or the child, contact local law enforcement and follow safety guidance from your attorney.

