- Short-term (weeks–few months)
  - Exchange of initial disclosures/financial documents.
  - Possible temporary orders hearing if immediate custody/support is contested.
  - Mediation or settlement conference may be scheduled.

- Mid-term (3–9 months)
  - Discovery (document production, written questions, depositions) and any evaluations (custody evaluation, psychological).
  - Motions (e.g., motions to compel, motions for temporary relief).

- Long-term (6–18+ months)
  - Settlement negotiations; if no settlement, pretrial conference and trial.
  - After trial, orders (custody/support) and potential post-trial motions or appeals.

