- Within weeks: exchange of initial disclosures and financial documents; possible filing of motions for temporary orders.
- 1–3 months: mediation/conciliation session(s), parenting evaluations may be ordered or proposed.
- 3–6 months: discovery continues; depositions or expert evaluations if ordered.
- 6+ months: settlement negotiations or trial scheduling (timeline varies widely with county backlog).
Note: timelines vary by county and judge. Ask your attorney for a local estimate.

