I can help you get organized for the next steps and for your meeting with Robert Kim. Before I give a detailed checklist and questions, one important clarification: you mentioned proceedings at family court in Denver and also Hennepin County, Minnesota. Which court actually has the case (Denver or Hennepin County)? Jurisdiction matters for procedure and timing, so tell me which one and I’ll tailor things more precisely. For now I’ll give a general, practical checklist and a focused list of questions to ask your attorney that apply in most U.S. custody/support/divorce matters.

Quick note: I’m not a lawyer — use this to structure your conversation with Robert Kim and get the legal advice you need from him.

Top items to confirm with your attorney (short list)
- Which court has jurisdiction (Denver or Hennepin County)? Where exactly is the status conference scheduled?  
- What is the precise date/time/location and what filings or documents must be filed before the status conference?  
- What does the attorney recommend as your primary goals for the status conference (scheduling, temporary orders, mediation referral, settlement discussions, etc.)?

Detailed questions to ask Robert Kim (grouped by topic)

Case status & court procedure
- What is the purpose of the status conference in this jurisdiction and what outcomes can we expect (scheduling orders, deadlines, temporary orders, referral to mediation/parenting evaluation)?  
- What deadlines will the court likely set at or after the status conference (discovery cutoff, expert disclosures, pretrial conference, trial date)?  
- What filings or forms do I need to complete before the conference (financial affidavits, proposed parenting plan, temporary order motions)?  
- How long is the typical timeline from status conference to trial in this county?

Jurisdiction & venue
- Confirm which court has jurisdiction and whether venue is proper. If there’s a jurisdictional dispute, what are our options?  
- If the other parent lives in a different state, how will that affect custody/support proceedings?

Custody (legal and physical)
- How does this court define legal vs. physical custody and how are decision-making and parenting time usually allocated?  
- Based on my circumstances, what custody arrangements are realistic? What factors will the judge consider most important?  
- Should we request a temporary parenting plan now? If so, what should it propose?  
- If there are safety or domestic-violence concerns, how do we raise them and get protective or supervised-visitation orders?

Child support & financial issues
- How is child support calculated here (income included, deviations, shared parenting formulas)?  
- Will we need a child support worksheet, and what income documents will the court require?  
- If spousal support is an issue, how does the court evaluate need/duration/amount?

Temporary orders & emergency relief
- Should we file for temporary custody/support/possession orders now? What is the strategic timing?  
- If I need emergency relief (e.g., immediate change in custody or protection), what steps do we take and do we have grounds?

Discovery & evidence
- What discovery will be required (financial disclosures, tax returns, employment records, communications, social media, school/medical records)?  
- Do we need to issue subpoenas, depositions, or expert reports? Who will handle obtaining them?  
- What evidence will be most persuasive for custody and support (school records, parenting logs, witness statements, mental health records)?

Evaluations & experts
- Will the court likely order a custody evaluation, guardian ad litem, parenting coordinator, or forensic accountant? How long do those take and what is the cost?  
- Do we need to propose experts or can we ask the court to order one? Who pays?

Mediation, settlement & negotiation
- Is mediation required or recommended before trial? What are the mediation procedures/local providers?  
- What settlement strategy do you recommend and what are realistic settlement ranges for custody/support in this case?

Trial preparation & costs
- What does trial look like here (length, witnesses, exhibits, live testimony vs. reports)?  
- What is an estimated timeline/fee estimate for litigation through trial vs settlement?  
- How do we manage costs (budget, phased approach, critical filings first)?

Parenting time logistics & relocation
- How are holiday/transportation/relocation disputes handled?  
- If either parent wants to relocate with the child, what rules and notice requirements apply?

Enforcement & modification
- How are temporary orders enforced? If the other parent violates an order, what remedies exist (contempt, enforcement motion)?  
- What are the standards and timing to modify custody or support later?

Practical communication & strategy
- How should I communicate with the other parent, with the court, and with you (email, text, portal)? Should I keep records of all contacts?  
- What behavior or actions should I avoid that might harm my case?  
