I can help — that’s a lot to manage, and it’s smart to go in prepared. First, two quick clarifying questions so I tailor this precisely:

- Which court is handling this matter: family court in Denver (Colorado) or Hennepin County, Minnesota? (You mentioned both.)
- Do you already have any temporary orders in place (custody/parenting time, child support, protection orders)?  
- How old are the children (minor/ages)? Any urgent safety concerns (domestic violence, substance use, threats)?

Below is a practical list you can use with your attorney (Robert Kim) and a checklist of documents and steps to prepare for the status conference and the next phases.

What to ask your attorney — prioritized and grouped

1. Immediate / before the status conference
- What is the judge likely to ask at the status conference and what do you want me to bring or be ready to say?  
- Should we seek any temporary orders now (custody, parenting time, child support, exclusive use of the home, protection)? If so, what’s the strategy and timeline?  
- Are there any immediate steps I should take to protect my rights or the children before the conference?

2. Case posture, schedule, and next steps
- What typical timeline should I expect (after status conference) for discovery, mediation, custody evaluations, and trial in this jurisdiction?  
- What deadlines will likely be set at the status conference (discovery, motions, mediation, settlement conference, expert disclosures, trial date)?  
- How do you recommend we schedule and prioritize tasks between now and the status conference?

3. Custody / parenting-time issues
- What custody outcomes are realistic given the facts of our case and local legal standards? (Ask attorney to frame specifically for the county/judge.)  
- How do we document parenting time and the parent-child relationship (logs, school/medical records, witnesses)?  
- If the other parent is seeking or has asked for supervision/parenting-time restrictions, what evidence will be needed to oppose or respond?

4. Child support and finances
- How is child support likely to be calculated here (what worksheets and income components count)? What documents should I gather?  
